<!-- ORIGIN — why / what / who (added 8/22) -->
<section class="vh-origin" id="origin">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px;text-align:center;padding:56px 0 44px">
    <div style="font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B6A3E;font-weight:600">Where CSH came from</div>
    <h2 style="margin:12px 0 16px">Advice from the operator&rsquo;s side of the table.</h2>
    <p style="max-width:60ch;margin:0 auto 22px;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.6">CSH Vault is what happens when the person advising you has actually run the companies, built the projects, and raised the money: 2,000+ homes, a quarter-billion in equity and tax credits sourced, and the scars to show where it&rsquo;s really won or lost. Not a broker. Not a lender. Someone holding the whole board with you &mdash; the assets, the capital, and the decisions behind them.</p>
    <a href="#" class="btn btn-primary" data-open-origin style="display:inline-block">Read the story (2 min)</a>
  </div>
</section>
<div id="vh-origin-modal" aria-hidden="true" style="position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:2147483000;display:none">
  <div data-close-origin style="position:absolute;inset:0;background:rgba(0,0,0,.74)"></div>
  <div role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Where CSH came from" style="position:relative;width:min(760px,94vw);margin:5vh auto;background:#14161c;color:#f3efe6;border:1px solid #2c303a;border-radius:14px;padding:40px 44px 34px;max-height:88vh;overflow:auto;font-family:Georgia,'Fraunces',serif;box-shadow:0 30px 90px rgba(0,0,0,.55)">
    <button type="button" data-close-origin aria-label="Close" style="position:absolute;top:8px;right:14px;background:none;border:0;font-size:30px;line-height:1;color:#a9adb6;cursor:pointer;padding:2px 8px">&times;</button>
    <p style="font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c9a96e;margin:0 0 10px">Where CSH came from</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:2rem;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 18px;color:#f3efe6;font-weight:500">Advice from the operator&rsquo;s side of the table.</h2>
    <div class="vh-origin-body" style="font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.7;font-weight:300"><p>I spent my career on the operating side &mdash; as executive director of a 501(c)(3) housing developer, as board president of a national resident-services nonprofit, as an officer of a property-management company, as general partner on dozens of partnerships, and as the attorney who closed them. More than $300 million in assets. A quarter-billion in private equity and tax credits. Two thousand homes. And the lesson every one of those years taught: the deal is never just the deal. It is the asset, the money, the program, the people, and the pressure, all at once &mdash; and most advisors only see one of them.</p><p>Brokers are paid on the transaction. Lenders are paid on the loan. Lawyers are paid on the documents. Someone has to see the whole board &mdash; and tell you, before capital is committed, where the thing actually breaks.</p><p>CSH Vault is that seat &mdash; and it is more than real estate. Development, asset decisions, capital strategy, partnerships, the business behind the holdings: whether to build, buy, hold, sell, restructure, or walk away. An independent, operator-led partner who pressure-tests the move, coordinates the licensed specialists each decision needs, and keeps one advisor holding the whole picture. If it touches your assets or the money behind them, it belongs in this conversation. We also publish reports on what we see coming, because the best advice starts with seeing ahead.</p><p>CSH is one of four practices under <a href="https://www.vaulthuman.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vault Human</a> &mdash; a family of companies built on the idea that a life, and a portfolio, should be held whole rather than handed out in pieces. The essay that started it is called <a href="https://www.vaulthuman.com/writing/the-fracture" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Fracture</a>.</p><p style="margin-top:22px">&mdash; Russ Michaels</p></div>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;margin-top:26px">
      <a href="#start" data-close-origin data-open-form style="display:inline-block;padding:12px 22px;border:1px solid #c9a96e;border-radius:6px;color:#14161c;background:#c9a96e;text-decoration:none;font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;font-weight:600">Start a conversation</a>
      <a href="https://www.vaulthuman.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:inline-block;padding:12px 22px;border:1px solid #8B9299;border-radius:6px;color:#f3efe6;text-decoration:none;font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif">Vault Human &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
